- op: discuss  # 46b9
  at: '2026-04-20T01:15:06Z'  # 46b9
  by: agent  # 46b9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 46b9
  clock: 4  # 46b9
  nonce: 46b9  # 46b9
  message: "Acknowledged — approved for governance file modification with auto-pr (no --gov gate). Using the Plan tool next turn to design the implementation before coding.\n\nConcrete plan sketch for the Plan-tool pass to refine:\n\n1. AGENTS.md addition: new subsection 'Bakeoff Validation Discipline' under Required Checks. Contents: the rule that any merged PR whose description or tracker discussion contains a quantitative bakeoff claim receives the 'awaits_bakeoff_validation' tag at merge time; an enumerated trigger vocabulary ('should improve', 'expected FP reduction', 'N dead → alive', 'NN% reduction', 'below threshold X', 'newly-consumed concept'); a note that 'scripts/tracker list --tag awaits_bakeoff_validation' is the authoritative running list of pending validations (replaces the stale WI-sofom hand-maintained pattern).\n\n2. bakeoff-deep-reflect aggregate cross-reference: at aggregate time, shell out to 'scripts/tracker list --tag awaits_bakeoff_validation --status todo_soft,in_progress --json' and intersect each item's claim text with the cohort's diag output areas (linker names, language names, tier labels). For each overlap, inject a per-claim question into the reflect prompt: 'Did metric X move for area Y as claimed in <item-ID>?' The prompt's structured-response schema gets a new per-claim-verdict field: moved / no_move / inconclusive. On 'moved': auto-strip the tag and post a tracker discuss entry with the evidence. On 'no_move': create a regression sub-item under the original item and leave the tag in place.\n\n3. Stop-hook nudge: when 'tracker list --tag awaits_bakeoff_validation' ≥ threshold (start at 5) AND no bakeoff cycle completed in the last 72h, the hook surfaces 'N items await bakeoff validation; consider running a DEEP cycle'. Threshold + window tunable in .agent/stop_guidance_config.json.\n\n4. Acceptance demo: a full cycle where a new PR with a quantitative claim gets auto-tagged at merge (via an auto-pr hook), survives through the next bakeoff aggregation, and either loses the tag (metric moved) or spawns a regression sub-item (metric didn't move).\n\nOut-of-scope per the item: the retroactive apply (already done), orthogonal bakeoff execution.\n\nWill start with the Plan tool next turn; status stays todo_soft."  # 46b9
- op: discuss  # d258
