  clock: 5  # d258
  nonce: d258  # d258
  message: "Slice 1 landed and merged to dev (AGENTS.md 'Bakeoff Validation Discipline' section, commit 5895000b0). Scope:\n\n- Codified the discipline rule under Required Checks — enumerated trigger verb-set ('should improve X by N%', 'expected FP reduction', 'N dead → alive', 'NN% reduction', 'below threshold X', 'newly-consumed concept'), explicit 'what does NOT count' list (qualitative / coverage-deltas / unrelated perf).\n- Documented the authoritative running-list command (scripts/tracker list --tag awaits_bakeoff_validation), formally superseding the stale WI-sofom hand-maintained pattern.\n- Forward reference to the reflect-aggregate cross-reference glue (slice 2) so the discipline is in force independently of the tooling.\n\nRemaining slices per the plan:\n- Slice 2: bakeoff-deep-reflect aggregate cross-references. Shell out to 'tracker list --tag awaits_bakeoff_validation --status todo_soft,in_progress --json' at aggregation time; inject per-claim questions into the reflect prompt schema (moved / no_move / inconclusive); auto-strip the tag or spawn a regression sub-item based on the verdict.\n- Slice 3: stop-hook nudge. Surface 'N items await bakeoff validation' when the tag count exceeds a threshold (propose 5) and no DEEP cycle has run in the last 72h. Threshold and window in .agent/stop_guidance_config.json.\n- Slice 4: acceptance demo. Full cycle where a newly-merged PR with a quantitative claim gets auto-tagged, survives a DEEP cycle, and either loses the tag (metric moved) or spawns a regression sub-item.\n\nI'll keep this item todo_soft — slices 2/3/4 are natural follow-ons but not blocked by each other. Happy to continue picking them up as sessions allow."  # d258
